red_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T11:54:12Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T12:19:22Z","body":"But they already look differenlty in a few ways. So I don't think that the color must be the same.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b7a3cdb6-01d7-4668-a4db-01c4800b1de8)\r\n\r\nAlso, when you add an internal vertex, you lose the ability to view and edit it in the scene view. So making the highlighted color of internal vertices the same, as in scene view, is impossible (because there're no internal vertices in the scene view).\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a675d197-2327-4e4f-9958-5f02355daa38)\r\n\r\nA much closer reference is the AnimationPlayer editor. But it applies the same (or almost the same) color, that the Polygon2D editor uses for unhighlighted internal vertices:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/381c85f6-da31-431d-85f8-d6e1c3e2bcc4\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2996185420/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2996414674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107890#issuecomment-2996414674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107890","id":2996414674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ymajS","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T13:02:35Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T13:12:25Z","body":"The main performance problem of Polygon2D editor is because it still uses the inefficient canvas draw functions for every single line and handle texture, aka every single vertex edge segment is its own canvas item and draw in the editor. It basically creates a new throwaway mesh for every single handle point that it deletes on the next redraw, oc performance is bad with that on larger polygons.\r\n\r\nShould be switched to use static meshes and multimeshes like done for Path2D editor in PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105606","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2996414674/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2996621245","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107890#issuecomment-2996621245","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine